# Translation script for set.mm. Syntax, axioms, and variables are
# translated automatically, so the script only says how far to go and lists
# fixups (skip LABEL, assume LABEL, replace LABEL followed by copied lines
# ending with --, bound_form LABEL...).
#
# This currently covers propositional and predicate calculus, stopping
# before ZF set theory.

# These theorems need two setvars that bind to be the same variable at some
# step of their proof, which Ghilbert doesn't allow (bound variables are
# always distinct). Their translated statements are still true (they only
# add distinctness), so they are assumed until someone writes new proofs.
assume exexw
assume aev2
assume hbaev
assume naev
assume hbnaev
assume axc16
assume dral1v
assume axc11n
assume dral1ALT
assume nfald2
assume 2ax6elem
assume 2ax6e
assume axc16gALT
assume nfsb4t
assume sbidm
assume sbco2
assume sbco3
assume sb9
assume nfsbd
assume sbal2
assume eujustALT
assume exists2
assume axbnd

run_until ax-ext
